        "state": "complete",
        "role": "coordinator",
        "max_iterations": 8,
        "outcome": "success",
        "result": "{\"action\":\"respond_direct\",\"reason\":\"For IoT edge deployments on constrained ARM devices, MQTT has the edge on raw latency and footprint (Mosquitto runs under 2MB resident; QoS 0 publishes complete in well under a millisecond on Raspberry Pi-class hardware). NATS wins when you need both pub/sub AND request-reply in the same broker \u2014 its subject hierarchy is more expressive and JetStream gives you persistence \u2014 but it costs ~30MB of resident memory which matters on the tightest devices. Pick MQTT if pub/sub alone is sufficient and memory is tight; pick NATS when the workload needs request-reply or you have \\u003e256MB RAM to spare. The full research artifact (actors, integration points, decision criteria) is captured in the chain entity for follow-up.\"}"
